@startuml retrieval
!include style.puml
skinparam ranksep 28

rectangle "**Rewritten query**" as Q0 $accentBg

rectangle "**1 · Hybrid search**\n<size:11><color:$dim>dense vectors + BM25 keywords,</color></size>\n<size:11><color:$dim>weighted blend over 1,566 chunks</color></size>" as S1
rectangle "**2 · Cross-encoder rerank**\n<size:11><color:$dim>an ONNX model scores each</color></size>\n<size:11><color:$dim>query–candidate pair</color></size>" as S2
rectangle "**3 · Multi-hop**\n<size:11><color:$dim>follows real cross-reference</color></size>\n<size:11><color:$dim>links between documents</color></size>" as S3
rectangle "**4 · Context assembly**\n<size:11><color:$dim>per-document cap, trace</color></size>\n<size:11><color:$dim>expansion, character budget</color></size>" as S4

rectangle "**Context**\n<size:11><color:$dim>handed to the synthesizer</color></size>" as OUT $goodBg

Q0 -down-> S1
S1 -down-> S2 : <color:$good>**+0.063 recall**</color>
S2 -down-> S3 : <color:$good>**+0.031 MRR**</color>
S3 -down-> S4 : <color:$good>**hit rate → 1.000**</color>
S4 -down-> OUT

note right of S1
  The biggest single win, and the
  cheapest. Exact tokens like
  PAY-5021 are what a dense
  embedding blurs away.
end note

note right of S2
  Buys ranking, not recall — and
  costs 50x the latency. That is
  the trade, measured rather
  than assumed.
end note

note right of S3
  Closes the last gap: every golden
  question now has its evidence
  somewhere in the context.
end note
@enduml
